What the hell happened here? ==================================================================
What the hell happened here? codegen.memeasm - the code generator: writes the assembly text of the analysed program
What the hell happened here? Reimplements translator.rs and asm_text.rs of the reference compiler for its `-S` output:
What the hell happened here? Linux target, martyrdom on, no -O level, no debug info, one input file (file index 0).
What the hell happened here? Monke label prefix of this file: uua. Edition / function prefix: gen.
What the hell happened here? ==================================================================
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? How the text is printed
What the hell happened here? -----------------------
What the hell happened here? Every byte goes through `what can I say except`. Constant texts are packed into 64 bit numbers,
What the hell happened here? eight bytes per number, the first byte in the lowest bits ("little endian"): the number for
What the hell happened here? "ab" is 97 + 98 * 256 = 25185. genEmit1 prints the bytes of such a number from the lowest one
What the hell happened here? up and stops when the rest is 0, so a number holds 1 to 8 bytes. genEmit2 .. genEmit5 print
What the hell happened here? two to five numbers (rdi, rsi, rdx, rcx, r8) one after the other: up to 40 bytes per call.
What the hell happened here? Above every packed number (or group of numbers) a comment shows the text it prints.
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? The current command
What the hell happened here? -------------------
What the hell happened here? While the commands are translated, rbx points to the record of the current command (layout
What the hell happened here? in DESIGN.md). The helpers of this file read rbx but never change it (it is callee-saved anyway).
What the hell happened here?   record + 0 OPCODE, + 16 POINTER, + 24 TRANSLATE, + 64 / 128 / 192 the parameters
What the hell happened here?   parameter + 0 TEXT, + 8 LEN, + 16 TYPE, + 24 VALUE, + 32 VERBATIM, + 40 ESCAPE
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? The layout rules of asm_text.rs boil down to this for one file without -O and debug info:
What the hell happened here? * a function definition is "name:" in the first column,
What the hell happened here? * every line of every other command starts with a tab, also its labels ("\t.Luau:") and its
What the hell happened here?   numeric local labels, which share the line with the next instruction ("\t1: xor rax, rax")
What the hell happened here?   or stand alone if nothing follows them in the command ("\t1:"),
What the hell happened here? * some commands end with a line that holds only the tab ("gap" in translator.rs).
What the hell happened here? So instead of an indentation state and pending labels, every command prints its exact text.
